From 040d23df39a6d0f92f5a0fed092f69085a4e669a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:32:40 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_printer_manager: Device list that waits for CUPS before
 it says anything
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device (docs/page-design.md): list of printers and groups, each opens its own page (kcm.push), page
actions at the top right. The existing structure already matched, so only these changes; CUPS calls, the
command-line arguments (add-printer, add-group, configure-printer) and the printer pages are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- "Add…" -> "Add Printer…" (kcm_printer_manager/AddPrinter), now the real visible label, not only the accessible name.
- Empty state "No printers are currently set up" gets an "Add Printer…" button and no longer appears before CUPS has
  answered (kcm_printer_manager/NoPrinters); a spinner shows only after 150 ms.
- Markers only (labels unchanged) on 46 rows in the sub-pages (printer page, driver chooser, find printer,
  server settings, install dialog) so --strict can prove them: 54 rows, 0 lost.
- inventory/relabel/kcm_printer_manager.tsv (outer repo).

Speed (read from code):
- The CUPS list is already asynchronous (PrinterModel::update uses KCupsRequest, a worker thread); the first frame was
  held by main.qml's `visible: !kcm.isSCPAvailable()`, which called ListActivatableNames (every activatable bus name)
  synchronously during page creation. Now PrinterManager::scpMissing is filled by an async call in the constructor
  (isSCPAvailable() stays for SCPInstaller).
- Before the first CUPS reply the model state is Unknown, but the empty-state Loader treated "count == 0" as "no
  printers": it flashed the wrong message. Now it waits for the state.
- FindPrinter device discovery and the PPD list are only started on their sub-pages (checked: not created by main.qml).
After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-020 (empty state with action).

Not built yet. Uncertain: the banner for the missing helper now appears after the reply, not at creation.
Sub-page labels (printer page "Queue Name:" etc.) were not reworded in this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
